  "notes": "Premier modern historical-comparative lexical reconstruction establishing Proto-Tangkhulic etymological roots and sound correspondences across divergent village varieties. Authorized under CC-BY-NC 4.0.",
  "alternate_title": "Comparative Tangkhul and Proto-Tangkhulic Lexicon",
  "background": "Developed by linguist David R. Mortensen at the University of California, Berkeley (2003/2012) and incorporated into the Sino-Tibetan Etymological Dictionary and Thesaurus (STEDT) project under Prof. James A. Matisoff. Represents the most comprehensive comparative linguistic reconstruction of the Tangkhulic language subgroup, documenting phonological sound laws, reconstructed Proto-Tangkhulic (PTk) starred forms, and multi-dialectal cognate sets across Ukhrul, Kachai, Huishu, Champhung, and Tusom varieties.",
  "phonology_notes": "Features reconstructed Proto-Tangkhulic phonological forms (*kʰa-matʰa, *ŋa-wa, *si-ruy) and establishes rigorous tone correspondence laws across northern, southern, and central Tangkhulic lects.",
